      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the context before improving understandability.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n1. Many unused imports (serialization classes, `Arrays`, `ScratchBytes`, `ScratchChars`, unused assertion methods)\n2. No explanation of what each assertion group tests\n3. No messages on assertions to describe intent\n4. Missing `@DisplayName` annotation\n\nI'll write an improved version that removes clutter, adds assertion messages, groups assertions with explanatory comments, and adds a display name — without changing any runtime behavior.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes unused imports, adds a `@DisplayName` annotation, groups assertions by `IOCase` mode with explanatory comments, and adds per-assertion messages — all without changing any method calls, arguments, or expected outcomes."
